    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Development began in 1912 when Joseph A. Allen’s land company purchased 1,000 acres of the Wichita River valley for resale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamay%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Oil exploration drove the town’s growth, with the K‑M‑A Oil Company—named after the three investors’ surnames—established in the 1920s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamay%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town boasted 27 businesses by the mid‑1950s, reflecting its early commercial vitality.",
